# Your keys and passwords. Never commit these.
#
# The pattern matches a file called exactly `.env`, at any depth - so
# `API_V1/database/.env` and `API_V1/dashboard/standard/.env` are covered, while `.env.example`
# (which documents every variable) and `API_V1/database/.env.test` (a throw-away
# archive on 127.0.0.1 whose password protects nothing) are NOT, and both
# are committed on purpose. Do not "tidy" this into `.env*`: that would
# swallow the two files a fresh clone needs to run the tests.
.env
.env.bak-labels

# Python
__pycache__/
*.py[cod]
.venv/
.pytest_cache/

# Editors
.idea/
.vscode/

# Working files of an AI-assisted project setup (AGENTS.md): test documents,
# expectations and the results of each round. They are the person's material,
# not part of this repository.
setup/
